 "_about_normalize": "How a raw handle becomes the form the map stores. The store script applies this to what Kevin types; the channel applies it to the sender BlueBubbles reports, after dropping a service prefix like `iMessage:`, before looking the handle up. `want` null means the handle is refused. Every handle is made up. A bare 10-digit number is taken as North American (+1): true for this family, but a number from elsewhere written without its country code is mapped wrong rather than refused. BlueBubbles 1.9.9 reports handle.address as +1 and 10 digits, and uncanonicalizedId as the bare 10 digits (Esme's probe, 2026-11-18).",
